usiness_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","review_id":"BAsxXpCJLE752o164ihfhA","date":"2017-03-07T07:47:32","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9450550079345703,"text_excerpt":"Saw this as we were walking around the French Quarter and I knew I had to get me some Popeyes while in NOLA! Walked in and it was an incredibly awkward setup!! In the middle of the restaurant, there's a counter but that's not where you order. You walk further to the end where there are barriers that split into two lines where you can order on either side. There wasn't a menu posted - guess you just know when you come here? Ordered some fries, chicken and biscuits. Nothing to crazy as they were pretty much closing. The lady at the counter was really sweet and directed us to the awkward middle counter to get our food packed up to go. It took wayyy longer than it should have but I was very h..."},{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","review_id":"YFiutPcnAeBz9qWIW40P7g","date":"2019-11-24T19:54:00","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.941338300704956,"text_excerpt":"The Popeyes restaurants in NOLA have food that tastes better. I've been visiting them here since the 80's. Earlier this month, we were in NOLA w/ family. Kids wanted a snack and Popeyes was nearby and appealing to the group. We walked in from Canal St and noticed that the wait was minimal. As they were ordering, I saw that the chicken sandwich was available. This was a bit shocking as there has been pandemonium around ATL for those hoping to try the elusive sandwich. I had to have one. Ordered it spicy. It came out quickly and I was excited to have the opportunity to snag one so easily. As you can see in the photo, it has the look of a typical chicken sandwich. Comes w/ pickles and a spic..."},{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","review_id":"vTukyNDSNO_YpXs9P-KeYA","date":"2013-02-01T02:14:08","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9400234818458557,"text_excerpt":"Yes, I am giving a fast food restaurant 4 star, in fact 4.5 star. Seriously how could Popeyes in New Orleans be soooo good?! Their Cajun fries have this delicious peppery taste, after adding their in-house hot spice, OMG that just turned sooo good. Their chicken was not overly fried either, perfect for my craving. Servers were extremely nice... HELLO, southern people! I love your kindnes. Conclusion: I love New Orleans' Popeyes. =D"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","photo_id":"Q6tg7bI7m_LKewJxg1a7rA","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/Q6tg7bI7m_LKewJxg1a7rA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9106613397598267},{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","photo_id":"mRpi3DEJ3okQ4UFoodTvZA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/mRpi3DEJ3okQ4UFoodTvZA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8400575518608093},{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","photo_id":"Oe2n9qBquKD5DgB-rOS0Ig","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Oe2n9qBquKD5DgB-rOS0Ig.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8314656019210815},{"business_id":"JIxyIXx5GmB2kSnBaRVPOg","photo_id":"Km262XnaxTRxqfAFoLYMhA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Km262XnaxTRxqfAFoLYMhA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8258825540542603}]},"notebook_case":null}
